<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>Staging table</title>
    <style>
        h3 { ${REGULAR_LARGE_FONT_STYLE} }
        body { ${REGULAR_FONT_STYLE} }
        code { ${MONOSPACE_FONT_STYLE} }
        h3 code { font-size: inherit; }
        p { margin-top:0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h3>Operating Mode</h3>
    <p>Choose how the assistant operates. Select the most appropriate mode for your use case:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>DEVELOPMENT</strong> – For database and code-focused work.
            <ul>
                <li>Use database, schema, table, view, and program metadata to explore structures</li>
                <li>Inspect view and program source code to understand existing logic</li>
                <li>Work in dataset, source code, and SQL console editors to draft and refine code</li>
            </ul>
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>ANALYTICS</strong> – For data exploration and querying.
            <ul>
                <li>Use database, schema, table, and view metadata to understand your data model</li>
                <li>Review view definitions to see how analytic layers are built</li>
                <li>Shape datasets and refine read-focused queries using dataset and SQL console editors</li>
            </ul>
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)</strong> – For semantic search–based answers.
            <ul>
                <li>Ask natural language questions over your indexed content</li>
                <li>Retrieve and summarize relevant information using semantic search</li>
                <li>Receive concise answers grounded in the retrieved material</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
    </ul>
</body>
</html>


